{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Motivation\n\nThe README is a feature list plus key tables, and docs/config.md is schema-oriented. The KDL config is hard to learn on your own — layers, merge rules, layout trees, `slot` `when`/`then`, presets, `\"None\"` unbinds, `pages`, `projects-board`, repo-local trust. A guide that teaches it step by step is needed.\n\n## Publishing decision\n\n- **Source of truth: in-repo Markdown** under `docs/guide/` — PR-reviewed, versioned with the code, and the config examples can be **CI-verified** (extract fenced config blocks and load each with `vig --config`; no broken examples ever ship).\n- **Rendering: mdBook → GitHub Pages** (`book.toml` + `SUMMARY.md` over the same files; an Actions workflow deploys on push to `main`; checkout needs `lfs: true` for the GIFs). Japanese version as a second book under `/ja/` — **not a follow-up: every chapter ships in English and Japanese together**, same as README / docs/README.ja.md.\n- **No wiki**: it versions separately from the code, bypasses PR review, and its examples cannot be CI-checked — the opposite of the tape-as-docs philosophy.\n- Published version tracks `main` only (per-tag docs if demand appears).\n\n## Chapters (draft)\n\n1. **Getting Started** — install, first run, a tour of the seven views (reusing the demo GIFs), `?` help\n2. **Views** — one section per view: what it shows, keys, constraints (the read-only philosophy lives here)\n3. **Configuration Basics** — file locations and layers (builtin → user → `.vig.kdl`), `vig config dump / path / themes / trust`, the \"copy the dump, then trim\" workflow, minimal KDL syntax\n4. **Config Recipes** (the hard parts, by example) — change theme/icons/image-preview; rebind one key, unbind with `\"None\"`, how presets work; trim/reorder tabs with `pages`; layout trees: reading `split` / `place` / `size` → resizing a pane → unplacing a pane → `slot` `when`/`then` (using the GitHub detail switch as the worked example); pin a board with `projects-board`, bring the Projects list pane back; repo-local `.vig.kdl` and the trust model\n5. **Config Reference** — every node (absorbing and restructuring docs/config.md): form / default / merge rule / example / error example\n6. **Troubleshooting / FAQ** — reading config errors (fail-fast philosophy), gh auth and the `project` scope, rate limits, no Nerd Font, cache locations and clearing\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] Chapter skeleton + Getting Started + Views\n- [ ] Configuration Basics + Recipes (highest value)\n- [ ] Fold docs/config.md into the Reference; fix inbound links\n- [ ] CI verification of guide config examples (extract fenced blocks → load with `--config`)\n- [ ] mdBook setup + Pages deploy workflow (`lfs: true`)\n- [ ] Japanese book under `/ja/` (each chapter lands together with its English counterpart)\n- [ ] README: shrink the Configuration section to a minimal example + a link to the guide\n\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-31T06:17:09Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvQg","name":"documentation","description":"Improvements or additions to documentation","color":"0075ca"},{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":136,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Detailed user guide (docs/guide) rendered with mdBook on GitHub Pages"}
